# FeF3, rhombohedral ReO3-type, space group R-3c (#167), ambient-pressure
# phase (Leblanc et al. 1985 cell, via rhombohedral a=5.362 A / alpha=57.94 deg
# converted to hexagonal a=5.196 A / c=13.309 A).
#
# Confirmed against Data/FeF3/r3c 20.txt directly: indexed the 8 clearest
# real peaks (2theta = 23.98, 33.62, 34.66, 40.32, 48.89, 54.42, 55.83,
# 61.21) against this space group with Cu Ka1 (1.54059 A, per user: the
# r3c dataset was collected on a copper source, not synchrotron -- the
# project's original ws2.prm, at 0.3344 A, belongs to the OTHER dataset
# (Data/MgO+MgBC), whose D8_parameter-1.prm already has 1.54059/1.54442
# Cu Ka1/Ka2, i.e. the two instrument files were swapped between datasets).
# A grid search over (a_hex, c_hex) at this wavelength found a=5.19,
# c=13.23 as the best geometric match -- every one of the 8 peaks matched
# a calculated reflection within 0.13 deg, most within 0.01-0.08 deg. That
# refined cell is within ~1% of the literature ambient-pressure value used
# here. The project's original CIF (fef3 r3c.cif / .fixed.cif) used a
# rhombohedral cell about 3-4% larger (a=5.467, alpha=58.93) that does not
# match this indexing, and was very likely derived using the same wrong
# (synchrotron) wavelength assumption.
#
# F position reused from COD 2100647 (high-pressure FeF3, same space
# group/structure type) as a starting approximation for the octahedral
# tilt angle -- the two phases share space group and connectivity, so this
# is a reasonable starting point for Rietveld refinement, not claimed to
# be the exact ambient-phase value; expect the Cell stage (and, if used,
# --refine-atoms) to adjust it further.
data_FeF3_ambient
_cell_length_a                   5.196
_cell_length_b                   5.196
_cell_length_c                   13.309
_cell_angle_alpha                90.0
_cell_angle_beta                 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma                120.0
_space_group_name_H-M_alt        'R -3 c'
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M   'R -3 c'
_space_group_IT_number           167
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number      167

loop_
   _atom_site_label
   _atom_site_occupancy
   _atom_site_fract_x
   _atom_site_fract_y
   _atom_site_fract_z
   _atom_site_adp_type
   _atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv
   _atom_site_type_symbol
   Fe1   1.0   0.0      0.0   0.0    Uiso  0.19  Fe
   F1    1.0   0.3441   0.0   0.75   Uiso  0.30  F
